---
description: "Project security guardrails (always on)"
alwaysApply: true
---

Security guardrails for this project. Always apply.

- Never log secrets, credentials, session tokens, API keys, raw hashes,
  recovered passwords, or other sensitive payloads.
- Never disable transport security (TLS/mTLS, signature checks) outside of
  the explicit dev compose / dev profile.
- Treat all uploaded files, rules, wordlists, and user content as
  untrusted: enforce size caps, validate types, and reject path traversal.
- Never invoke subprocesses with `shell=True` or string-concatenated
  commands; always pass an argv list and validate arguments.
- Pin external binary versions (hashcat, ffmpeg, etc.) by digest or tag
  when correctness depends on the binary version.
- Sensitive data at rest must be encrypted with a project-approved
  primitive; do not invent crypto.
- Surface authn/authz failures the same way for unknown vs wrong-credential
  cases to avoid enumeration.
- Stop and ask before adding a new outbound network call from a
  privileged context.
